            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_2",
            "review_title": "Review at La Focaccia",
            "review_text": "Patricia T\nTunis, Tunisia21 contributions\n0\nBest pizza in Tunis\nJan 2018 • Couples\nThis is the best pizza in Tunis, hands down. Thin crust, excellent and fresh ingredients, and very reasonably priced. Living here for a year, I have searched far and wide for Italian or Italian-American style pizza in Tunis and this place is by far the most authentic. We visit once (and sometimes twice) a week and the quality never varies. My husband (Tunisian) enjoys the Cippolla pizza (tuna and onions) and I (American) have a fondness for the Primavera (with fresh arugula, real Parma Grana cheese, and fresh tomatoes) and the pies that have Gorgonzola. Everything on the menu is between 10-18 Dinars (approximately $5-$9 USD) and is a large, personal size pizza that feeds one very hungry person or two moderately hungry people. The staff here is also fabulous. Friendly, very professional and always welcoming. Arabic, French, and some English and Italian spoken. We visit the one in Menzah 5 although there are two other locations. It is tiny (6 tables) and often busy but well worth the wait. There's a decent ice cream shop next door as well. Highly recommend, especially for any homesick Americans or Italians looking for a good pizza with real Italian ingredients.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 17, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
